.TH REDROBIN 1 "September 2026" "Red Robin 0.1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
redrobin \- configurable network connectivity and diagnostics tester

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redrobin
.RB [ \-c " FILE" ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.br
.B redrobin
.B \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Red Robin
is a configurable command-line network connectivity and diagnostics
tester for Linux.

It can test multiple network connection methods and present the results
in a human-readable three-column display.

The default display contains:

.IP \(bu 2
the location or connection target,
.IP \(bu 2
a friendly connection rating,
.IP \(bu 2
technical connection statistics.

The friendly ratings are:

.TP
.B YUM
The connection is performing within the configured healthy range.

.TP
.B MEH
The connection works but is outside the preferred latency range.

.TP
.B YUCK
The connection failed or exceeded the configured poor-performance
threshold.

The rating is intended as a quick human-readable summary.
The technical statistics remain the authoritative diagnostic information.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " FILE"
Use a specific YAML configuration file.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show additional information about individual tests.

.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Show only failed tests.

.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output results as JSON.

.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the Red Robin version.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help.

.SH CONFIGURATION

When no configuration file is supplied, Red Robin checks:

.nf
~/.config/redrobin/config.yml
.fi

If that file does not exist, Red Robin uses its built-in default
configuration.

The configuration file uses YAML.

Example:

.nf
settings:
  timeout_seconds: 3
  retries: 2
  parallel: true

tests:
  - name: "Cloudflare DNS"
    type: "icmp"
    target: "1.1.1.1"
.fi

.SH TEST TYPES

Red Robin supports or is designed to support the following test types:

.IP \(bu 2
.B icmp
.IP \(bu 2
.B tcp
.IP \(bu 2
.B udp
.IP \(bu 2
.B dns
.IP \(bu 2
.B http
.IP \(bu 2
.B https
.IP \(bu 2
.B tls
.IP \(bu 2
.B tor
.IP \(bu 2
.B onion
.IP \(bu 2
.B i2p

Individual test types may require a local service, appropriate network
access, or additional system configuration.

.SH EXAMPLES

Test using the default configuration:

.nf
redrobin
.fi

Use a custom configuration:

.nf
redrobin --config ~/my-redrobin.yml
.fi

Show verbose information:

.nf
redrobin --verbose
.fi

Output JSON:

.nf
redrobin --json
.fi

Show command help:

.nf
redrobin --help
.fi

.SH FILES

.TP
.I ~/.config/redrobin/config.yml
Per-user Red Robin configuration.

.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/redrobin.1
System manual page when installed system-wide.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
All configured tests completed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
At least one configured test failed.

.TP
.B other
The program could not start or encountered a fatal configuration or
runtime error.

.SH NOTES

ICMP tests normally require the
.B ping
program to be installed.

Some systems restrict ICMP access for unprivileged applications.
A failed ICMP test therefore does not necessarily indicate that the
entire Internet connection is unavailable.

UDP services may intentionally ignore unsolicited packets. A failed
generic UDP test should therefore be interpreted together with its
technical statistics.

